the surprise announcement came in a  televised speech sunday night vladimir  zielinski suspending two of the most  powerful people in his government  just last thursday irina benedictova was  representing ukraine in the hague  coordinating with other countries over  investigations into war crimes as  ukraine's prosecutor general benedictova  has been a high profile and vocal figure  she's been front and center the other  suspended official hasn't had quite the  same profile but he does have very close  ties to zielinski himself ivan bakanov  was the head of the sbu ukraine spy  agency but he and zelensky were  childhood friends and he ran zielenski's  presidential campaign  zielinski suspended the two saying  members of their agencies are suspected  of conspiring with russia he said there  are 651 cases of alleged treason and  collaboration being investigated clearly  the russians have been  building this capability they have tried  to undermine the ukrainian government  the ukrainian state for a long time  now russia is applying a different  pressure on other european countries  this week russian gas exporter gazprom  sent out letters to several customers  declaring something called force measure  it means it won't be able to send as  much fuel as it was contracted to send  due to something out of its control it's  a sort of active god clause there is  fear russia could move to cut off  supplies completely countries are now  trying to refill storage sites before  winter and the heating season mike  armstrong global news
 

